Subject: [PATCH 7/8] Fix findings of the second fresh-copy verification

- multimodal_baseline.md step 5 writes the re-extraction to a new prefix, because the cache
  archive now ships reproduction_distilbert_first_token under the recorded name.
- summarize_multimodal_runs: document --pattern '20261016_*' to reproduce the committed
  table (the default also lists the 42 sweep runs).
- checkpoints.md: the two 20261001 image heads need --features_dir as well as
  --reference_metrics; the train/validation ROC-AUC caveat names the heads its ranges
  come from.
- Known problems: validation loss is lowest at epoch 1 in the 2026-10-16 runs (within the
  first 5 epochs in the sweep).
- Multimodal_Assets.md: the run-output archive omits the whole review/ folder; the
  summary script counts folders with metrics_validation.json.
- /model shows local encoder copies as local_dir:<folder> (api_spec.md updated).
- .dockerignore excludes data, checkpoints, outputs, logs, caches and weight/archive
  formats at any depth (src/features/ stays in the context).
- Image docs: PowerShell route A starts from the merged cache archive; remaining
  references to the image group's branches name the original team repository.
- Multimodal_Test_Results.md: 2026-10-18 record of the fresh-copy verification.

